# TacoWP (registry server)

This repo is the **self-hosted private plugin registry** (Next.js + Prisma + PostgreSQL). The sibling WordPress worker is `wp-plugin-private-updater`. The server reads private GitHub releases via a GitHub App and forwards ZIP downloads and remote commands to licensed sites.

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing APIs, auth, GitHub sync, or the site ping protocol.

- Admin dashboard and most `/api/v1/*` admin routes: NextAuth session.
- WordPress client routes (`update-check`, `download`, `heartbeat`, `license/validate`, `plugins/available`): license key + site URL.
- Command poll/result: `siteToken`. Push to a site: HMAC ping to the **front page**, never `/wp-admin/` (WP Engine will block PHP writes).
- Plugins are GitHub repos; latest release is cached on `Plugin`. Sites never talk to GitHub.
- Domain: Plugin, Site, License, SitePlugin, Command — see `prisma/schema.prisma`.
